ents first right and we've been  proud of the uh 29 28 billion dollars in  loan forgiveness up to this point and  the policies that we've changed to fix a  broken system so uh we recognize  americans are waiting on that and we're  going to be uh communicating with them  as soon as we can  can i ask you about teacher salaries  again because everybody always says  teachers need to make more money they  should be paid i don't know anybody who  disagrees with you but that never  changes so what is it going to take for  teachers to make more money in this  country who do we need to tell who do  you need to call what do we need to do  look remember during the omicron surge  where  our schools were closed because our  educators had to quarantine  yes remember the disruption that that  caused across our communities across our  country  let's not go there again we're at the  doorstep of a crisis and if we're not  taking this seriously if that wasn't a  warning that we need to really lift the  profession and  pay them competitive salaries especially  when the job market is what it is then  we're we're missing an opportunity here  so but who makes governors  who makes their decision well state  education funding right state education  funding is is the place to start the  federal government makes up about 10  percent of education funding in general  look at the increases that we put in it  not only with arp but in our yearly  budget i want the same level of urgency  from governors and from uh county and  city leaders across the country  yeah  it's not only pay either it's uh freedom  to teach a lot of teachers feel that  they are in these very narrow lanes  being watched very closely and it's a  dangerous profession to be a part of  that's part of a longer conversation  though secretary cardona thank you very  much
 

